@startuml Sequence - Patient Registration
title Patient Registration Flow (API Documentation)

actor Patient
participant "API Gateway\n(Ingress)" as gateway
participant "Auth-Service" as auth
participant "Clients-Service" as clients
database "Auth DB\n(H2)" as auth_db
database "Clients DB\n(H2)" as clients_db

Patient -> gateway: POST /auth/register\n{name, email, password, role=PATIENT}
gateway -> auth: Forward to /auth/register
auth -> auth: Validate password & email uniqueness
auth -> auth_db: Save User (email, password, role)
auth -> clients: POST /patients/internal\n{userId, name, birthDate, phone, insuranceInfo, consent}\n(Header: X-INTERNAL-KEY)
clients -> clients_db: Save Patient
clients --> auth: Patient created
auth --> gateway: Return JWT token
gateway --> Patient: Registration successful + token

note right: API: /auth/register (POST) - Registers user & patient.\n/auth/login (POST) - Authenticates & returns JWT.
@enduml
